    slug: "spider-man-brand-new-day-gise-rekoru-onizleme",
    title: "\"Spider-Man: Brand New Day\" Breaks Box Office Record With $72 Million in Previews",
    excerpt: "Tom Holland's new Spider-Man film grossed $72 million in previews, shattering \"Avengers: Endgame\"'s $60 million record.",
    body: "'Spider-Man: Brand New Day' has already spun a web through box office history on its very first day.\n\nTom Holland's new Spider-Man film earned $72 million in previews, including Wednesday's early-access screenings — the highest preview haul in cinema history. The previous record belonged to 'Avengers: Endgame,' which went on to become the biggest opening weekend of all time; that film made $60 million in its Thursday previews.\n\nDirected by Destin Daniel Cretton, the film reunites Holland with Zendaya and Jacob Batalon. The fourth installment following 2021's 'No Way Home,' which grossed $1.9 billion worldwide, finds Peter Parker starting over from scratch in a world where no one remembers him.\n\nFor Sony and Marvel, this number has also lifted expectations for the rest of the summer season; analysts have already begun raising their opening-weekend forecasts.",
    image: "https://variety.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/MCDSPMA_SP142.jpg?w=1000&h=667&crop=1",
